*   **Charitable Donation ($800):** This is deductible, but *only* if you itemize your deductions (see below).
*   **Self-Employment Deductions:** You can deduct half of your self-employment tax (calculated on your $15,000 freelance income) as an adjustment to income.

### 2. How to Treat the Home Office
Because you have freelance income (web design) and an exclusive home office, you can deduct home office expenses against your $15,000 self-employment income. You have two options:
*   **Simplified Method:** $5 per square foot up to 300 sq ft. (165 sq ft × $5 = **$825 deduction**).
*   **Actual Expenses Method:** You calculate the percentage of your home used for business (165 sq ft ÷ 690 sq ft = **23.91%**). You can deduct 23.91% of your rent ($1,720 × 12 = $20,640/year × 23.91% = **$4,935 deduction**). You can also add 23.91% of your renter's insurance, utilities, and internet. 
*   **Recommendation:** The Actual Expenses method will give you a significantly larger deduction (over $4,900 vs. $825), lowering your taxable freelance income and your self-employment tax.

### 3. Itemize vs. Standard Deduction
For 2023, the **Standard Deduction for a single filer is $13,850**. 
